{
  "$comment": "T-241 negative golden. Identical to golden-missions/last-stand-at-montfort.json except the boundary zone's `graceSeconds` is misspelled `graceSecconds`. This is the fixture that pins the whole `zones[].rules` vocabulary: before T-241 `rules` was {\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":true} with zero declared properties, and this document validated CLEAN (measured \u2014 `xtask schema validate-file` returned ok against the pre-T-241 schema). Delete `additionalProperties: false` from #/$defs/zoneRules, or drop any one of the sixteen declared keys, and this file starts passing, which fails the run. Why a MISSPELLING rather than a bad value: both readers are TYPED \u2014 Enfusion's `JsonLoadContext` maps JSON keys onto named class fields, so a key no class declares is invisible to the mod rather than rejected. `TBD_ZoneRegistry.ResolveRules` cannot even report it honestly (its diagnostic is worded to cover both \"authored nothing\" and \"authored a key this build cannot see\", because a typed parser genuinely cannot tell those apart). The schema is therefore the ONLY place in the system where this class of defect can be caught at all. See README.md for the wrapper format \u2014 this is NOT a mission document.",
  "mustFail": {
    "gate": "schema",
    "at": "/zones/4/rules",
    "because": "a misspelled rule key is invisible to the typed mod reader, so this boundary silently runs on the 30 s default grace instead of the 20 s the author wrote \u2014 and its penalty is `kill`, so the mistake is paid for with a player's only life 10 s earlier than intended"
  },
